me>Kung</surname><given-names>AL</given-names></name><name><surname>Zabludoff</surname><given-names>SD</given-names></name><name><surname>France</surname><given-names>DS</given-names></name><name><surname>Friedmann</surname><given-names>SJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Tanner</surname><given-names>EA</given-names></name><name><surname>Vieira</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Cornell-Kennon</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Lee</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Wang</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Wang</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Memmert</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Naegeli</surname><given-names>HU</given-names></name><name><surname>Petersen</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Eck</surname><given-names>MJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Bair</surname><given-names>KW</given-names></name><name><surname>Wood</surname><given-names>AW</given-names></name><name><surname>Livingston</surname><given-names>DM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Small molecule blockade of transcriptional coactivation of the hypoxia-inducible factor pathway</article-title><source>Cancer Cell</source><year>2004</year><volume>6</volume><fpage>33</fpage><lpage>43</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15261140</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.ccr.2004.06.009</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Vordermark</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Shibata</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Brown</surname><given-names>JM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Green fluorescent protein is a suitable reporter of tumor hypoxia despite an oxygen requirement for chromophore formation</article-title><source>Neoplasia</source><year>2001</year><volume>3</vo